## 8. Source Preservation

When actual source documents are supplied, the ingestion workflow must preserve their substantive contents.

Do not replace the original document with an AI-generated summary.

Preserve:

- Original sections.
- Heading hierarchy.
- Tables.
- Lists.
- Decision identifiers.
- Requirement identifiers.
- Original terminology.
- Architectural constraints.
- Source links.
- Explicit uncertainties.
- Deferred decisions.
- Approval statements.
- Historical notes.
- Applicable copyright notices.

It is acceptable to add presentation metadata and a YAML frontmatter envelope.

Any substantive editorial correction must be separately identified.

Do not silently rewrite an original source.

Source documents may contain stale or conflicting information.

Preserve the original material and identify verified discrepancies separately rather than altering historical evidence.

